            <ArticleTitle>Comparison of cholesterol in habitually high and low active school-age children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While risk-factor screening programs for coronary artery disease have been effective among adults, few programs are available for school-age children. 31 children were screened (16 active and 15 inactive) for cholesterol levels. The physically active group had a nonsignificantly lower mean which may reflect the small sample.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
